    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Ok, I see. I was specifically looking at the seismic activity section in the geological report, though. It mentions some concerns about soil liquefaction during minor tremors. Given how much pressure there is to get this approved for the city's development, does that liquefaction risk actually pose a dealbreaker, or is it something that can just be managed with standard building codes?",
